docs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md:17:| [`qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex`](qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex) | `lem:qld-4-13`, chapter 14 lines 1020--1034 | `lem:qld-4-13`, `rem:qld-4-13-source-defects`, `lem:qld-4-13-established` | Source statement kept as printed; the unproved `poly(m^2 epsilon, md/q)` form is tracked in the proof and the remark, while the established `m * poly(epsilon, md/q)` bound is derived in the proof, used in the sequel, and stated as a separate formalization-support node. | Neither declaration matches its source or blueprint statement. Both return `ExtendedLinesWitness`, whose extended questions come from the directly indexed line space at dimension `2m+2`, whose average is the directly indexed line-point law, and whose two consistency displays compare `Option`-completed answers instead of summing over `a` in `F_q`; only the error forms are as advertised over that replacement -- `poly(m^2 epsilon, md/q)` for `exists_extendedLinesWitness` and `C m poly(epsilon, md/q)` for `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established`. Accordingly neither `lem:qld-4-13` nor `lem:qld-4-13-established` carries a statement-level `\leanok`, and both proofs are open. The two-variable error functions of all four declarations, and of the two `lem:qld-xz-lines` carriers `exists_combinedLinesWitness` and its `_ofPointsWitness` companion, are quantified by the shared predicate `IsPolyErr₂`, which since the correction recorded in [`qpbt_pasting-product-error.tex`](qpbt_pasting-product-error.tex) states the sum bound `C (x^r + y^s)` on the closed nonnegative quadrant rather than the source's product form; the printed error expressions of `lem:qld-4-13` and `lem:qld-xz-lines` are qualified accordingly in the blueprint and in the docstrings of the six declarations. | [#173](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/173) |
docs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md:22:| [`qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`](qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex) | `lem:qld-sublines`, `lem:qld-4-7`, and the `lem:ld-soundness` import | `lem:ld-soundness`, `lem:qld-sublines`, `lem:qld-4-7`, `rem:qld-4-7-divisibility` | The blueprint keeps `lem:qld-sublines`, `lem:qld-4-13`, and `lem:qld-4-7` in their source shape over the seed-indexed line-point distribution on `F_q^{2m+2}`, adds no divisibility hypothesis, and marks the blocked steps in the proofs, in `rem:qld-4-7-divisibility`, and in the soundness-import node, instead of adding the impossible condition `2m+2 | q`. The directly indexed extended line space remains a Lean-side replacement and is described in the formalization-support node `lem:qld-4-13-established`; it is not adopted as the carrier of source-shaped `lem:qld-4-13`, whose existing witness link remains marked `\notready`. | The Lean carriers realize dimension `2m+2` by direct index sampling, so they are defined for every admissible tuple, but they are not the seed-indexed objects of the source-labelled blueprint nodes. `exists_direct_ld_soundness` proves soundness of the directly indexed game through `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.mainFormal`; at each combined LDT dimension `M` it uses `N = 2560000 M^3 d` and proves that theorem's distinct condition `400 M d <= N`. The correlated-residue lift preserves projectivity and game value, and diagonal-block compression preserves the two mixed consistency defects. Separate compression does not preserve the global/global defect: the lifted state pairs equal residues whereas separate compression averages two residues independently. For `k = 1`, `exists_ld_soundness_of_k_eq_one` recovers that relation on the original Hilbert spaces using point agreement and Schwartz--Zippel, completing seed-indexed soundness; `exists_direct_ld_soundness_of_k_eq_one` retains its direct specialization. The general-`k` seed-indexed theorem remains open. This direct route does not apply the tensor-code theorem and therefore does not discharge the original source-import obligations: the claimed tensor-code game correspondence and the requirement `K >= 12 m (d + 1)` for the printed choice `K = m^3 d` remain open, as do the construction proofs of `lem:qld-4-7`. | [#18](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/18), [#173](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/173) |

